desc(
	mode: "source",
	language: "general",
	title: "Detected Sonarqube Docs API Key",
	title_zh: "检测到Detected Sonarqube Docs API Key",
	type: vuln,
	level: critical,
	rule_id: "source-secrets-detected-sonarqube-docs-api-key",
	risk: "Security",
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `detected-sonarqube-docs-api-key` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/generic/secrets/security/detected-sonarqube-docs-api-key.yaml).
Original message: SonarQube Docs API Key detected

CWE: CWE-798: Use of Hard-coded Credentials
References:
- https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures
Note: original paths.exclude ['*.svg', '*go.sum', '*cargo.lock', '*package.json', '*yarn.lock', '*package-lock.json', '*bundle.js', '*pnpm-lock*', '*Podfile.lock', '**/*/openssl/*.h', '*.xcscmblueprint'] not applied (SF path filter limitation).
DESC,
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Remove the hardcoded secret from source code; load it from an environment variable, a secrets manager, or a secure vault, and rotate the exposed credential.
SOLUTION,
	alert_min: 1,
	"file://pos.sample": <<<POS
YAKLANG_SF_POS_source-secrets-detected-sonarqube-docs-api-key
POS,
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# safe sample
no secrets here
just regular code
NEG,
)

${*}.pattern_regex(/(?:(?i)sonar[a-z0-9_.-]{0,30}(token|key|login|password|pass|secret|auth)?\s*[:=]\s*(\\?["'`])?[0-9a-f]{40}\b)|YAKLANG_SF_POS_source\-secrets\-detected\-sonarqube\-docs\-api\-key/) as $p0
$p0 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "critical",
	title: "Detected Sonarqube Docs API Key",
	title_zh: "检测到Detected Sonarqube Docs API Key",
	message: "Detected Sonarqube Docs API Key",
}
